{
  "scope": "One cysteine-hydrolase input cys_pair_1; local RTX A4000, B1 D1, 200 schedule points, full memory; no additional refolds",
  "conclusions": [
    "GPU-CPU synchronization removal preserved every captured noise, schedule, checked initializer, trajectory, final-coordinate and logit tensor exactly in the controlled same-process comparison.",
    "The baseline repeated exactly within that process. Cached topology changes the compiled trajectory even with native kernels.",
    "Cached and uncached eager denoisers returned bitwise-identical output on the same captured real input. Selected atom/token neighbor indices and masks also matched in eight checks. Their compiled outputs differ.",
    "The custom transition follows eager BF16 rounding; default compiled PyTorch elides intermediate rounding. Isolated 128-channel tests match eager and rounding-preserving compilation exactly, but differ by about 0.36 percent relative L2 from default compilation.",
    "The native and custom-transition full-rollout means were essentially equal at local B1; baseline repetitions varied substantially. This is not evidence of a robust large local speedup.",
    "The four-pair pilot does not establish a quality regression or equivalence. Different generated backbones produced different LigandMPNN sequences; downstream sequence RNG was only seeded once per arm.",
    "Fresh-process baseline replay was not exact despite identical feature hashes; the original run did not save initial-coordinate tensors or full state. That discrepancy is not yet isolated and prevents calling these exact reproductions of the original pilot."
  ],
